The files in this directory are derived from the following sources.

1. Gender Representation in Video Games
   Author: Palomar (Kaggle user "Brisa", br33sa), 2022
   Source: https://www.kaggle.com/datasets/br33sa/gender-representation-in-video-games
   License: CC BY-NC 4.0

   Files: raw/kaggle_games.csv, raw/kaggle_characters.csv and
   raw/kaggle_sexualization.csv are copies of the original tables, re-saved
   without changes to their content (games.grivg.csv, characters.grivg.csv
   and sexualization.grivg.csv).
   processed/games.csv and processed/characters.csv are ADAPTED versions:
   the games were filtered to those with a Metacritic score of at least 80 on
   RAWG, integrated with RAWG metadata by normalized title, deduplicated by
   game (one edition per game), and supplemented with derived columns
   (numeric percentages and renamed score fields); the character table was
   restricted to the selected games and joined with the sexualization
   dimensions. See notebooks/01_data_processing.ipynb for every step.

2. RAWG Video Games Database API
   Source: https://rawg.io/apidocs (data from RAWG, https://rawg.io)
   Files: raw/rawg_games_raw.csv and raw/rawg_collection_info.json
   (collection of 28 September 2026). RAWG data remain subject to the RAWG
   API terms of use.

The adapted data in processed/ are licensed under CC BY-NC 4.0 as well.
They may be shared and adapted for NON-COMMERCIAL purposes only, with
attribution to the original authors listed above and an indication of any
further changes. No warranties are given.
